From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 19:06:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03329/11362] [outer-loop] arc: cell-recall trust gate fires
 the prior+TTT path 4/5 on unseen games (was 0/5)

The exact-full-grid-match trust gate killed the TTT path on every unseen game (LOO 0/5) -- a
64x64 CNN is ~55% changed-cell-accurate but ~0% exact-grid. Added a granularity-matched
trust_cell_recall metric (changed-cell recall) + trust_metric param on
gated_engine_from_transitions (default stays 'exact' -> live agent + existing tests unchanged).
Re-running the LOO probe: cell-recall gate fires WARM 4/5 vs SCRATCH 2/5 -- the warm-start prior
adds +2 firings (tn36 0.14->0.87, lp85 0.32->0.59 cross 0.5 only with the prior) and strengthens
ka59/sc25. cd82 (134 trans, too small) stays below. The dynamics genuinely transferred; the old
gate just couldn't see it. Firing is necessary-not-sufficient: whether a plan BFS'd through a
~0.6-0.9 cell-recall model actually SOLVES (+ goal-induction) is the next offline gate signal,
not settled here -- so trust_metric stays 'exact' in the live agent until solve-validated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
